    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "On the pair-Lagrange distance-three chart, multiplicativity against X^N-1=(X-s)(X-x_0)ABC gives an exact sparse factorization of the full subgroup norm. After multiplication by z, it is a nonzero explicit scalar times Q(z;s)Q(z;x_0)(z P_I)^r H(z). Under the external design, H=L P_Z^r, so the complete supported-slope locator z P_I P_Z appears to the exact power r. This reconstructs the active-row norm by exact division from a binomial-domain resultant and two boundary-row forms.",
